{"nbformat":4,"nbformat_minor":0,"metadata":{"colab":{"provenance":[],"collapsed_sections":["21_QA8sF48b3","erBj46E3xqFh","ZApjFRGJLHav"],"authorship_tag":"ABX9TyNLyzV1fXKkRsFlPrtPS1e9"},"kernelspec":{"name":"python3","display_name":"Python 3"},"language_info":{"name":"python"}},"cells":[{"cell_type":"markdown","source":["# **INTRODUCTION:**\n","\n","In this notebook, I explore the original SpaceNet 7 Multi-Temporal Urban Development Challenge Dataset before I clean the data to prepare it for my model training.  In my exploration, I display statistical analysis and visualizations relating to:\n","- the directory structure of the dataset\n","- statistics about the dataset's contents\n","- examination of data type specifics\n","\n","\n","***DATASET:*** https://spacenet.ai/sn7-challenge/\n","\n","Instructions for downloading the original dataset from AWS are provided at the link to the challenge's website above. After downloading the dataset, I have moved the base train, test_public, and csvs directories to the top level SpaceNet7 directory."],"metadata":{"id":"21_QA8sF48b3"}},{"cell_type":"markdown","source":["First, we will mount Google Drive to access the dataset."],"metadata":{"id":"mwnEOulw6nss"}},{"cell_type":"code","source":["from google.colab import drive\n","drive.mount('/gdrive')\n","\n","# Here we set the root_directory which will contain a string showing the path to the dataset.\n","root_dir = '/gdrive/My Drive/SpaceNet7'"],"metadata":{"colab":{"base_uri":"https://localhost:8080/"},"id":"WgPniFcb7mAI","executionInfo":{"status":"ok","timestamp":1712781845095,"user_tz":420,"elapsed":23270,"user":{"displayName":"Zachary Luttrell","userId":"00155576860657313600"}},"outputId":"723c1246-9aa8-454a-b92f-51035b09db07"},"execution_count":1,"outputs":[{"output_type":"stream","name":"stdout","text":["Mounted at /gdrive\n"]}]},{"cell_type":"markdown","source":["# **DIRECTORY STRUCTURE:**\n","Here we can see the directory structure of the base dataset.  \n","\n","In these tree visualizations below, we can see:\n","- The top level of the SpaceNet7 directory which contains the three main directories: train, test_public, and csvs.\n","- Inside our main directory, 'train', are 60 directories, each one for a different AOI\n","- The contents of one of these AOI directories, which are comprised of 6 main directories."],"metadata":{"id":"erBj46E3xqFh"}},{"cell_type":"code","source":["# reference for visualizing directory tree structures: https://stackoverflow.com/questions/9727673/list-directory-tree-structure-in-python\n","\n","from pathlib import Path\n","\n","# Set the root path for the tree visualizations\n","root_path = Path(root_dir)\n","\n","# TOP DIRECTORY TREE VISUALIZATION\n","def tree_root_only(dir_path: Path):\n","    \"\"\"Generates a tree for the root directory and its immediate subdirectories, including the root.\"\"\"\n","    print(dir_path)\n","    pointers = ['├── ', '└── ']\n","    contents = list(dir_path.iterdir())\n","    dirs = [d for d in contents if d.is_dir()]\n","\n","    for i, path in enumerate(dirs):\n","        pointer = pointers[0] if i < len(dirs) - 1 else pointers[1]\n","        print(pointer + path.name)\n","\n","# visualize the tree\n","print(f'Below is a tree showing the top level directory, SpaceNet7, which contains the 3 main directories that store our data.\\n')\n","tree_root_only(root_path)"],"metadata":{"colab":{"base_uri":"https://localhost:8080/"},"id":"2ggJXX_6pTCE","executionInfo":{"status":"ok","timestamp":1712781930967,"user_tz":420,"elapsed":201,"user":{"displayName":"Zachary Luttrell","userId":"00155576860657313600"}},"outputId":"2da2d6d0-7ec2-454c-94eb-e6a47bd5f323"},"execution_count":2,"outputs":[{"output_type":"stream","name":"stdout","text":["Below is a tree showing the top level directory, SpaceNet7, which contains the 3 main directories that store our data.\n","\n","/gdrive/My Drive/SpaceNet7\n","├── train\n","├── csvs\n","└── test_public\n"]}]},{"cell_type":"code","source":["## TRAIN