 AOI EXAMINATION VISUALIZATION\n","def tree_aoi_contents(dir_path: Path):\n","    \"\"\"Generates a tree for an AOI directory, showing all its subdirectories, including the AOI directory itself.\"\"\"\n","    print(dir_path)\n","    pointers = ['├── ', '└── ']\n","    contents = list(dir_path.iterdir())\n","    dirs = [d for d in contents if d.is_dir()]\n","\n","    for i, path in enumerate(dirs):\n","        pointer = pointers[0] if i < len(dirs) - 1 else pointers[1]\n","        print(pointer + path.name)\n","\n","# AOI visualization\n","print(f'NOTE: If this data exploration is taking place after training mask generation, there may be another directory named masks shown here.\\n')\n","print(f'Now, let us examine the contents of one of these AOI directories.\\nBelow, you can see that each AOI directory contains 5 major directories containing various data types.\\n')\n","tree_aoi_contents(root_path / 'train' / 'L15-0331E-1257N_1327_3160_13')\n","\n","def tree_aoi_contents_with_files(dir_path: Path, file_limit=3):\n","    \"\"\"Generates a tree for an AOI directory, showing all its subdirectories and up to three files per subdirectory, including the AOI directory itself.\"\"\"\n","    print(dir_path)\n","    pointers = ['├── ', '└── ']\n","    contents = list(dir_path.iterdir())\n","    dirs = [d for d in contents if d.is_dir()]\n","\n","    for i, subdir in enumerate(dirs):\n","        pointer = pointers[0] if i < len(dirs) - 1 else pointers[1]\n","        print(pointer + subdir.name)\n","\n","        # Now, let's list up to three files from this subdir\n","        files = list(subdir.iterdir())\n","        files_to_show = files[:file_limit]\n","\n","        for j, file in enumerate(files_to_show):\n","            file_pointer = '│   ├── ' if j < file_limit - 1 else '│   └── '\n","            if j == len(files_to_show) - 1 and len(files) > file_limit:\n","                print(file_pointer + file.name + \" (and more...)\")\n","            else:\n","                print(file_pointer + file.name)\n","\n","        if len(files) > file_limit:\n","            print('│   ...')\n","\n","# AOI + files visualization\n","print(f'\\nInside our directories are the files that we will use to extract the data necessary for training our model.\\nOur key interest is in the images_masked and the labels_match directories.\\n')\n","tree_aoi_contents_with_files(root_path / 'train' / 'L15-0331E-1257N_1327_3160_13')"],"metadata":{"colab":{"base_uri":"https://localhost:8080/"},"id":"0p5xb9Aqpl5n","executionInfo":{"status":"ok","timestamp":1712781958303,"user_tz":420,"elapsed":823,"user":{"displayName":"Zachary Luttrell","userId":"00155576860657313600"}},"outputId":"ba4a0c66-9506-4641-b554-59a85f976639"},"execution_count":4,"outputs":[{"output_type":"stream","name":"stdout","text":["NOTE: If this data exploration is taking place after training mask generation, there may be another directory named masks shown here.\n","\n","Now, let us examine the contents of one of these AOI directories.\n","Below, you can see that each AOI directory contains 5 major directories containing various data types.\n","\n","/gdrive/My Drive/SpaceNet7/train/L15-0331E-1257N_1327_3160_13\n","├── images\n","├── images_masked\n","├── labels_match_pix\n","├── labels\n","└── labels_match\n","\n","Inside our directories are the files that we will use to extract the data necessary for training our model.\n","Our key interest is in the images_masked and the labels_match directories.\n","\n","/gdrive/My Drive/SpaceNet7/train/L15-0331E-1257N_1327_3160_13\n","├── images\n","│   ├── global_monthly_2018_05_mosaic_L15-0331E-1257N_1327_3160_13.tif\n","│   ├── global_monthly_2019_02_mosaic_L15-0331E-1257N_1327_3160_13.tif\n","│   └── global_monthly_2019_05_mosaic_L15-0331E-1257N_1327_3160_13.tif (and more...)\n","│   ...\n","├── images_masked\n","│   ├── global_monthly_2018_02_mosaic_L15-0331E-1257N_1327_3160_13.tif\n","│   ├── global_monthly_2018_01_mosaic_L15-0331E-1257N_1327_3160_13.tif\n","│   └── global_monthly_2018_04_mosaic_L15-0331E-1257N_1327_3160_13.tif (and more...)\n","│   ...\n","├── labels_match_pix\n","│   ├── global_monthly_2018_01_mosaic_L15-0331E-1257N_1327_3160_13_Buildings.geojson\n","│   ├── global_monthly_2018_02_mosaic_L15-0331E-1257N_1327_3160_13_Buildings.geojson\n","│   └── global_monthly_2018_03_mosaic_L15-0331E-1257N_1327_3160_13_Buildings.geojson (and more...)\n","│   ...\n","├── labels\n","│   ├── global_monthly_2019_05_mosaic_L15-0331E-1257N_1327_3160_13_UDM.geojson\n","│   ├── global_monthly_2018_02_mosaic_L15-0331E-1257N_1327_3160_13_Buildings.geojson\n","│   └── global_monthly_2018_03_mosaic_L15-0331E-1257N_1327_3160_13_UDM.geojson (and more...)\n","│   ...\n","└── labels_match\n","│   ├── global_monthly_2018_01_mosaic_L15-0331E-1257N_1327_3160_13_Buildings.geojson\n","│   ├── global_monthly_2018_02_mosaic_L15-0331E-1257N_1327_3160_13_Buildings.geojson\n","│   └── global_monthly_2018_03_mosaic_L15-0331E-1257N_1327_3160_13_Buildings.geojson (and more...)\n","│   ...\n"]}]},{"cell_type":"markdown","source":["# **DATASET STATISTICS:**\n","In this section, I review some statistics to help get a sense of the dataset's shape.  The key interests within the dataset are the files that are found within the images_masked and labels_match directories.  These directories contain the masked images and matching building footprint geojsons that are generated from the combination of the base .tif imagery with the UDM masks subtracted out when applicable.\n","\n","By examining these statistics, my goal is to identify how much useable data I have to work with."],"metadata":{"id":"ZApjFRGJLHav"}},{"cell_type":"markdown","source":["**COUNTING THE TOTAL NUMBER OF IMAGES AND LABELS IN THE DATASET**\n","\n","In our dataset, we have 60 distinct AOIs.  Each AOI is supposed to have 24 image/label pairs, one for each month, over a two year timespan.\n","\n","> *60 AOIs x 24 image/label pairs = 1,440 image/label pairs*\n","\n","Knowing this, we should expect to find 1,440 images and 1,440 labels total. Also, I will check to see if any labels or images are missing their partner.\n"],"metadata":{"id":"JldvbkJA7B8V"}},{"cell_type":"code","source":["from pathlib import Path\n","\n","root_dir = Path('/gdrive/My Drive/SpaceNet7/train')\n","\n","def count_files_and_find_missing():\n","    total_tif = 0\n","    total_geojson = 0\n","    total_pairs = 0\n","    missing_images = 0\n","    missing_labels = 0\n","\n","    for aoi_dir in root_dir.iterdir():\n","        if aoi_dir.is_dir():\n","            images_masked_dir = aoi_dir / 'images_masked'\n","            labels_match_dir = aoi_dir / 'labels_match'\n","\n","            # Adjust the collection of image and label file names to account for the naming convention\n","            images = {f.stem: f for f in images_masked_dir.iterdir() if f.suffix == '.tif'}\n","            labels = {f.stem.replace('_Buildings', ''): f for f in labels_match_dir.iterdir() if f.suffix == '.geojson'}\n","\n","            # Update total counts\n","            total_tif += len(images)\n","            total_geojson += len(labels)\n","\n","            # Iterate over images to find matching labels\n","            for image_name in images:\n","                if image_name in labels:\n","                    total_pairs += 1\n","                else:\n","                    missing_labels += 1  # Count how many images don't have a matching label\n","\n","            # Check if there are labels without a matching image\n","            for label_name in labels:\n","                if label_name not in images:\n","                    missing_images += 1  # Count how many labels don't have a matching image\n","\n","    return total_tif, total_geojson, total_pairs, missing_images, missing_labels\n","\n","# Get the counts and print them out\n","total_tif, total_geojson, total_pairs, missing_images, missing_labels = count_files_and_find_missing()\n","print(f'TOTAL COUNTS:')\n","print(f\"Total .tif images: {total_tif}\")\n","print(f\"Total .geojson files: {total_geojson}\")\n","print(f\"Total matching pairs: {total_pairs}\")\n","\n","print(f'\\nMISSING PAIRS:')\n","print(f\"Images without a matching label: {missing_labels}\")\n","print(f\"Labels without a matching image: {missing_images}\")"],"metadata":{"colab":{"base_uri":"https://localhost:8080/"},"id":"HFQHNyxUNojZ","executionInfo":{"status":"ok","timestamp":1712782060389,"user_tz":420,"elapsed":30161,"user":{"displayName":"Zachary Luttrell","userId":"00155576860657313600"}},"outputId":"a8a36469-939a-4331-dc2d-17edd9273f66"},"execution_count":5,"outputs":[{"output_type":"stream","name":"stdout","text":["TOTAL COUNTS:\n","Total .tif images: 1423\n","Total .geojson files: 1423\n","Total matching pairs: 1423\n","\n","MISSING PAIRS:\n","Images without a matching label: 0\n","Labels without a matching image: 0\n"]}]},{"cell_type":"markdown","source":["**A FIRST LOOK AT MISSING DATA**\n","\n","From the output above, we can see that of the expected 1,440 image/label pairs, we only have 1,423 actual pairs.  While these missing 17 pairs may not be crucial to training a basic segmentation model which isn't concerned about a time-series of imagery, this is still something to keep in consideration in case a model with more of a temporal focus is pursued later.\n","\n","For now, I will attempt to identify which AOIs are missing values just to make a note of it."],"metadata":{"id":"1QnQm19c8_a5"}},{"cell_type":"code","source":["from pathlib import Path\n","from collections import defaultdict\n","\n","root_dir = Path('/gdrive/My Drive/SpaceNet7/train')  # Adjust as needed\n","\n","def find_aois_with_missing_pairs():\n","    expected_pairs_per_aoi = 24\n","    aois_missing_pairs = {}\n","\n","    for aoi_dir in root_dir.iterdir():\n","        if aoi_dir.is_dir():\n","            images_masked_dir = aoi_dir / 'images_masked'\n","            labels_match_dir = aoi_dir / 'labels_match'\n","\n","            # Adjust the collection of image and label file names to account for the naming convention\n","            images = {f.stem: f for f in images_masked_dir.iterdir() if f.suffix == '.tif'}\n","            labels = {f.stem.replace('_Buildings', ''): f for f in labels_match_dir.iterdir() if f.suffix == '.geojson'}\n","\n","            # Determine actual pairs based on matching criteria\n","            actual_pairs = sum(1 for image_name in images if image_name in labels)\n","            missing_pairs = expected_pairs_per_aoi - actual_pairs\n","\n","            if missing_pairs > 0:\n","                aois_missing_pairs[aoi_dir.name] = missing_pairs\n","\n","    return aois_missing_pairs\n","\n","# Populate and organize AOIs with missing pairs\n","aois_missing_pairs = find_aois_with_missing_pairs()\n","missing_groups = defaultdict(list)\n","for aoi, missing in aois_missing_pairs.items():\n","    missing_groups[missing].append(aoi)\n","\n","# Sort and print organized information\n","sorted_groups = dict(sorted(missing_groups.items(), reverse=True))\n","print(\"AOIs Missing Image/Label Pairs:\")\n","for missing, aois in sorted_groups.items():\n","    print(f\"Missing {missing}:\")\n","    for aoi in sorted(aois):\n","        print(f\"    {aoi}\")\n","\n","# Additional statistics\n","total_aois_missing_pairs = len(aois_missing_pairs)\n","total_missing_pairs = sum(aois_missing_pairs.values())\n","print(f'\\nADDITIONAL STATISTICS:')\n","print(f'Total AOIs Missing Pairs: {total_aois_missing_pairs}')\n","print(f'Total Missing Pairs: {total_missing_pairs}')\n"],"metadata":{"colab":{"base_uri":"https://localhost:8080/"},"id":"8m8E4KdBPR0-","executionInfo":{"status":"ok","timestamp":1712782097310,"user_tz":420,"elapsed":439,"user":{"displayName":"Zachary Luttrell","userId":"00155576860657313600"}},"outputId":"9bb128bd-4de0-489e-916f-3112ba0a24d3"},"execution_count":6,"outputs":[{"output_type":"stream","name":"stdout","text":["AOIs Missing Image/Label Pairs:\n","Missing 6:\n","    L15-1015E-1062N_4061_3941_13\n","    L15-1439E-1134N_5759_3655_13\n","    L15-1669E-1153N_6678_3579_13\n","Missing 4:\n","    L15-0571E-1075N_2287_3888_13\n","    L15-1538E-1163N_6154_3539_13\n","Missing 3:\n","    L15-0566E-1185N_2265_3451_13\n","    L15-0577E-1243N_2309_3217_13\n","    L15-0614E-0946N_2459_4406_13\n","Missing 2:\n","    L15-0387E-1276N_1549_3087_13\n","    L15-0683E-1006N_2732_4164_13\n","    L15-1438E-1134N_5753_3655_13\n","    L15-1709E-1112N_6838_3742_13\n","Missing 1:\n","    L15-0924E-1108N_3699_3757_13\n","    L15-1210E-1025N_4840_4088_13\n","    L15-1479E-1101N_5916_3785_13\n","    L15-1617E-1207N_6468_3360_13\n","\n","ADDITIONAL STATISTICS:\n","Total AOIs Missing Pairs: 16\n","Total Missing Pairs: 47\n"]}]},{"cell_type":"code","source":["import matplotlib.pyplot as plt\n","\n","def visualize_missing_pairs(aois_missing_pairs):\n","    # Sort AOIs by the number of missing pairs in descending order\n","    sorted_aois = dict(sorted(aois_missing_pairs.items(), key=lambda item: item[1], reverse=True))\n","\n","    aois = list(sorted_aois.keys())\n","    missing_pairs = list(sorted_aois.values())\n","\n","    plt.figure(figsize=(14, 8))\n","    bars = plt.bar(aois, missing_pairs, color='tomato')\n","\n","    plt.xlabel('AOI')\n","    plt.ylabel('Missing Pairs')\n","    plt.title('Missing Image/Label Pairs by AOI')\n","    plt.xticks(rotation=90)\n","    plt.tight_layout()\n","    plt.show()\n","\n","visualize_missing_pairs(aois_missing_pairs)\n","\n","\n","def visualize_distribution_of_missing_pairs(aois_missing_pairs):\n","    # Count how many AOIs fall into each category of missing pairs\n","    missing_categories = defaultdict(int)\n","    for missing in aois_missing_pairs.values():\n","        missing_categories[missing] += 1\n","\n","    # Prepare data for the pie chart\n","    labels = [f'Missing {k}' for k in sorted(missing_categories.keys())]\n","    sizes = [v for v in sorted(missing_categories.values())]\n","    colors = plt.cm.viridis(np.linspace(0, 1, len(labels)))\n","\n","    plt.figure(figsize=(8, 8))\n","    plt.pie(sizes, labels=labels, colors=colors, autopct='%1.1f%%', startangle=140)\n","    plt.axis('equal')\n","    plt.title('Distribution of AOIs by Number of Missing Pairs')\n","    plt.show()\n","\n","import numpy as np\n","visualize_distribution_of_missing_pairs(aois_missing_pairs)\n"],"metadata":{"colab":{"base_uri":"https://localhost:8080/","height":1000},"id":"xLPoje_xTHTt","executionInfo":{"status":"ok","timestamp":1712782113340,"user_tz":420,"elapsed":1069,"user":{"displayName":"Zachary Luttrell","userId":"00155576860657313600"}},"outputId":"a1a55dfa-312f-492b-e921-fe4edc0dc087"},"execution_count":7,"outputs":[{"output_type":"display_data","data":{"text/plain":["<Figure size 1400x800 with 1 Axes>"],"image/png":"\n"},"metadata":{}},{"output_type":"display_data","data":{"text/plain":["<Figure size 800x800 with 1 Axes>"],"image/png":"\n"},"metadata":{}}]},{"cell_type":"markdown","source":["**MISMATCH IN MISSING DATA**\n","\n","In my initial approach, I took the assumption that each location was expected to have 24 images, one per month, over a 2 year period, for 60 AOIs.  This would lead us to to assumption that there should be 1,440 total pairs of images and labels.  However, from my search above, we can see that, for each of the 60 AOIs, which we expect to contain 24 images, a total of 16 AOIs have less than the expected 24 pairs.  \n","\n","Totaling up how many pairs are missing by AOI gives us 47 missing pairs.  Since we saw in the analysis before that the dataset contains 1,423 total pairs, it is clear that there seem to be some additional pairs coming from somewhere.\n","\n","It is likely that some AOIs may contain more than the expected 24 pairs. To examine this further, I will perform a count of total pairs found within each AOI."],"metadata":{"id":"1OMC62aRFNvj"}},{"cell_type":"code","source":["from pathlib import Path\n","from collections import defaultdict\n","\n","root_dir = Path('/gdri