]},{"cell_type":"code","source":["import matplotlib.pyplot as plt\n","\n","def visualize_aoi_pair_counts(aoi_pair_counts):\n","    # Convert the AOI names and pair counts into lists for plotting\n","    aois = list(aoi_pair_counts.keys())\n","    pairs = list(aoi_pair_counts.values())\n","\n","    # Create a bar chart\n","    plt.figure(figsize=(14, 8))\n","    bars = plt.bar(aois, pairs, color='skyblue')  # Default color\n","\n","    # Add a horizontal line for the expected number of pairs\n","    plt.axhline(y=24, color='r', linestyle='-', label='Expected Number of Pairs (24)')\n","\n","    # Add labels and title\n","    plt.xlabel('AOI')\n","    plt.ylabel('# of Pairs')\n","    plt.title('Number of Image/Label Pairs by AOI')\n","    plt.xticks(rotation=90)  # Rotate AOI names for readability\n","\n","    # Color bars based on pair count\n","    for bar, pair_count in zip(bars, pairs):\n","        if pair_count < 24:\n","            bar.set_color('tomato')  # Below expected\n","        elif pair_count == 24:\n","            bar.set_color('mediumseagreen')  # Exactly meeting the expected\n","\n","    plt.legend()\n","    plt.tight_layout()  # Adjust layout to not cut off labels\n","    plt.show()\n","\n","# Visualize the AOI pair counts\n","visualize_aoi_pair_counts(sorted_aoi_pair_counts)\n"],"metadata":{"colab":{"base_uri":"https://localhost:8080/","height":807},"id":"t8qSQgSLQdTF","executionInfo":{"status":"ok","timestamp":1712782181539,"user_tz":420,"elapsed":1250,"user":{"displayName":"Zachary Luttrell","userId":"00155576860657313600"}},"outputId":"958f65d7-ad45-400a-f135-4da6abc80a2d"},"execution_count":9,"outputs":[{"output_type":"display_data","data":{"text/plain":["<Figure size 1400x800 with 1 Axes>"],"image/png":"\n"},"metadata":{}}]},{"cell_type":"code","source":["def visualize_aoi_distribution(aoi_pair_counts):\n","    # Count the categories\n","    more_than_24 = sum(1 for pairs in aoi_pair_counts.values() if pairs > 24)\n","    exactly_24 = sum(1 for pairs in aoi_pair_counts.values() if pairs == 24)\n","    less_than_24 = sum(1 for pairs in aoi_pair_counts.values() if pairs < 24)\n","\n","    # Labels for the categories\n","    labels = ['More than 24', 'Exactly 24', 'Less than 24']\n","\n","    # Corresponding sizes and colors\n","    sizes = [more_than_24, exactly_24, less_than_24]\n","    colors = ['skyblue', 'mediumseagreen', 'tomato']\n","\n","    # Create a pie chart\n","    plt.figure(figsize=(8, 8))\n","    plt.pie(sizes, labels=labels, colors=colors, autopct='%1.1f%%', startangle=140)\n","    plt.axis('equal')  # Equal aspect ratio ensures the pie chart is circular.\n","    plt.title('Distribution of AOIs by Pair Counts')\n","\n","    plt.show()\n","\n","# Visualize the distribution\n","visualize_aoi_distribution(sorted_aoi_pair_counts)"],"metadata":{"colab":{"base_uri":"https://localhost:8080/","height":675},"id":"tIsFDCW6Rcpl","executionInfo":{"status":"ok","timestamp":1712782278031,"user_tz":420,"elapsed":249,"user":{"displayName":"Zachary Luttrell","userId":"00155576860657313600"}},"outputId":"3e6fdee2-fe2d-41cd-e9da-14ca294a0041"},"execution_count":10,"outputs":[{"output_type":"display_data","data":{"text/plain":["<Figure size 800x800 with 1 Axes>"],"image/png":"\n"},"metadata":{}}]},{"cell_type":"markdown","source":["**FINAL NOTES**\n","\n","From this visualization, we can see that not only are some AOIs missing some of their 24 pairs, but also some AOIs contain more than the expected 24 pairs.  Upon visual inspection of the dataset, it appears that this is caused by mismatched time windows in which some AOIs have imagery with varying lengths of timespans.  This shouldn't effect our process for now, but is something to note.  In a sense, it may lead to a slight bias towards particular AOIs characteristics over less-represented AOIs, but the effect should not be too significant.\n","\n","Next, I move onto a deeper examination into our two main data types, .tif images and .geojson labels."],"metadata":{"id":"5OoDXiJMGpcY"}},{"cell_type":"markdown","source":["# **EXAMINATION OF DATA TYPES** (*'.tif'* and *'.geojson'*)**:**\n","\n","In this section, I will dive deeper into the specifics of both the .tif images and the .geojson labels.  I will examine the following types of things:\n","\n","*Images (.tif):*\n","- total range of sizes\n","- a visualization of each channel in an example .tif image\n","\n","*Labels (.geojson):*\n","- verification that labels contain geometries"],"metadata":{"id":"kChYeoTyyNTe"}},{"cell_type":"markdown","source":["**EXPLORING IMAGE SIZE RANGES**\n","\n","Here I take a look at the range of image sizes by directory.  We can see that images  in every directory range from a height of 1023-1024 and a width of 1023-1024.  \n","\n","To combat this, I will be patchifying the processed images into 256x256 patches during the data cleaning process, and will build the network to predict on this shape.  This will not only take care of the issue of mismatched image sizes, but will also increase the number of examples in our training data."],"metadata":{"id":"hGiSAkIutD4t"}},{"cell_type":"code","source":["from pathlib import Path\n","from PIL import Image\n","import numpy as np\n","\n","root_dir = Path('/gdrive/My Drive/SpaceNet7/train')  # Adjust path as needed\n","\n","def analyze_image_sizes_per_aoi(root_dir):\n","    aoi_ranges = {}\n","    all_sizes = []\n","\n","    for aoi_dir in root_dir.iterdir():\n","        if aoi_dir.is_dir():\n","            images_masked_dir = aoi_dir / 'images_masked'\n","\n","            for image_path in images_masked_dir.iterdir():\n","                with Image.open(image_path) as img:\n","                    size = img.size  # (width, height)\n","                    all_sizes.append(size)\n","\n","            if all_sizes:\n","                sizes = np.array(all_sizes)\n","                min_size = sizes.min(axis=0)\n","                max_size = sizes.max(axis=0)\n","                aoi_ranges[aoi_dir.name] = (min_size, max_size)\n","\n","    if all_sizes:\n","        total_sizes = np.array(all_sizes)\n","        total_min_size = total_sizes.min(axis=0)\n","        total_max_size = total_sizes.max(axis=0)\n","        total_range = (total_min_size, total_max_size)\n","    else:\n","        total_range = None\n","\n","    return aoi_ranges, total_range\n","\n","def print_aoi_size_ranges(aoi_ranges, total_range):\n","    print(f'{\"AOI:\":<40} {\"Image Size Range:\":>20}')\n","    for aoi, (min_size, max_size) in aoi_ranges.items():\n","        width_range = f\"[{min_size[0]} - {max_size[0]}]\"\n","        height_range = f\"[{min_size[1]} - {max_size[1]}]\"\n","        print(f'{aoi:<40} {width_range} x {height_range}')\n","\n","    if total_range:\n","        total_width_range = f\"[{total_range[0][0]} - {total_range[1][0]}]\"\n","        total_height_range = f\"[{total_range[0][1]} - {total_range[1][1]}]\"\n","        print(f'\\nTotal Size Range: {total_width_range} x {total_height_range}')\n","\n","# Running the analysis and printing the results\n","aoi_ranges, total_range = analyze_image_sizes_per_aoi(root_dir)\n","print_aoi_size_ranges(aoi_ranges, total_range)\n"],"metadata":{"colab":{"base_uri":"https://localhost:8080/"},"id":"oWToqdiKdMUs","executionInfo":{"status":"ok","timestamp":1712783355802,"user_tz":420,"elapsed":985474,"user":{"displayName":"Zachary Luttrell","userId":"00155576860657313600"}},"outputId":"f666bce1-66dd-414d-f50b-fad625ee2c76"},"execution_count":11,"outputs":[{"output_type":"stream","name":"stdout","text":["AOI:                                        Image Size Range:\n","L15-0358E-1220N_1433_3310_13             [1024 - 1024] x [1024 - 1024]\n","L15-0357E-1223N_1429_3296_13             [1024 - 1024] x [1023 - 1024]\n","L15-0331E-1257N_1327_3160_13             [1024 - 1024] x [1023 - 1024]\n","L15-0457E-1135N_1831_3648_13             [1024 - 1024] x [1023 - 1024]\n","L15-0368E-1245N_1474_3210_13             [1024 - 1024] x [1023 - 1024]\n","L15-0